        "kind": "requirement",
        "meaning": "If an employer does not maintain an accurate record of hours worked by an employee, the employer has the burden of showing that the employee has not worked the requisite hours to establish FMLA leave eligibility."
      },
      {
        "quote_ref": "F000",
        "scope_refs": [],
        "kind": "statement",
        "meaning": "The employer's burden of showing that an employee has not worked the requisite hours when accurate records are not maintained extends to employees who are exempt from the FLSA requirement to keep a record of hours worked, including bona fide executive, administrative, and professional employees as defined in 29 CFR part 541."
      },
      {
        "quote_ref": "F000",
        "scope_refs": [],
        "kind": "requirement",
        "meaning": "In order to claim that full-time teachers (as defined in § 825.102) of an elementary or secondary school system, institution of higher education, or other educational establishment or institution (who often work outside the classroom or at their homes) are not eligible for FMLA leave, an employer must be able to clearly demonstrate that they did not work 1,250 hours during the previous 12 months."
      },
      {
        "quote_ref": "F000",
        "scope_refs": [],
        "kind": "background",
        "meaning": "Directs to § 825.801(d) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees, serving solely as an informational cross-reference without establishing substantive standards here."
      }
